 "text": "Your goal didn't fail, your deadline was a guess. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 23. Arjun gives himself 4 weeks for his design portfolio. Week 4 it's half done, he feels behind so he stops opening it. We plan from the best case. In one study students guess their thesis would take 34 days, it took 56. The goal was fine, the date was wrong. So before you set a date ask, how long did the last thing like this take me? Arjun's last big project took 6 weeks so he plans 9. Now at week 4 it's half done, right on track. Send this to the friend who's always behind their own plan. That's what demure is for, archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, next, why reading about it feels like doing it. Which deadline are you behind on, the links in the bio?",
